preConditionHook:
// EL twin: on a month change (month(date) <> month(date[1])) set dayIndex to
// 1; otherwise, on a new date (date <> date[1]) with dayIndex already at least
// 1, add one to it.
//
// TRADING days, not calendar days. The source writes day(date) <= N, the day
// of the MONTH, which counts weekends and holidays -- and `dayofmonth` has no
// EL_FEATURES row in any case. dayIndex counts the distinct wall-clock DATES
// seen since the month rolled over, which is what "the first few trading days"
// means, and needs only `month` and `date`, both registered.
//
// `date` is the bar's wall-clock closing date, not its session date
// (EL_Date_Probe.txt: year/month/dayofmonth/dayofweek agree with
// civil_from_days(day_of(ctx.Time(0))) on 169/169 bars, 50 of them evening
// bars). date[1] is a DATA series with real history -- MaxBarsBack bars
// precede the strategy's first evaluated bar -- so ctx.Time(1) needs no
// first-bar guard, exactly as CalendarBoundaryExit notes.
//
// dayIndex is an EL VARIABLE and starts at 0, and the increment branch is
// gated on dayIndex >= 1, so it stays 0 until the first month boundary the
// strategy sees: the partial month at the chart start never fires.
//
// On a daily or 1440-minute series every bar is its own date, so dayIndex is
// the trading day of the month; on finer bars it holds at 1 for every bar of
// the month's first session.
curMonth = civil_from_days(day_of(ctx.Time(0))).month;
prevMonth = civil_from_days(day_of(ctx.Time(1))).month;
if (curMonth != prevMonth) {
    dayIndex = 1.0;
} else if (day_of(ctx.Time(0)) != day_of(ctx.Time(1)) && el_ge(dayIndex, 1)) {
    dayIndex = dayIndex + 1.0;
}
